{"name":"Chaps","hex":"#644b41","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Chaps","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["plural of Chap"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Chaps"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chaps","blocks":[{"text":"Chaparreras or chaps are a type of sturdy over-pants (overalls) or leggings that developed in Mexico from earlier Spanish equestrian and ranching traditions brought to America during the colonial era. Chaps are made of leather, without a seat, made up of two separate legs that are fastened to the waist with straps or belt. They are worn over trousers and were originally intended for protecting the rider from the rain and mud, and from tears and injuries. They were created to replace armas de agua or simply armas (shields), a set of leather flaps that hung from the Mexican saddle to protect the rider's legs from the rain. The word \"chaparreras\" is believed to have come from either “chaparrón”, a cloudburst or sudden, heavy rain, or from “chaparros”, a Mexican colloquial name for brush and a type of shrub. Due to the difficult pronunciation, Americans shortened the word to Chaps, originally spelled and pronounced schaps or shaps. Chivarras, from chivo (goat), is the name for chaparreras made of goatskins tanned with the hair on."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Chaps_-_colour_isolated.jpg/330px-Chaps_-_colour_isolated.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chaps"},{"title":"CHAPS","blocks":[{"text":"The Clearing House Automated Payment System (CHAPS) is a real-time gross settlement payment system used for sterling transactions in the United Kingdom. It is mainly used by financial institutions to make wholesale financial payments and by large companies to make corporate treasury payments. In 2024, 52.7 million CHAPS payments were made, worth a total of £87.5 trillion. This made up just 0.1% of the total number of payments in that year, but was 88% of the total value of payments."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CHAPS"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Charro%2C_Colecci%C3%B3n_Duque_de_Montpensier.jpg/500px-Charro%2C_Colecci%C3%B3n_Duque_de_Montpensier.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Charro%2C_Colecci%C3%B3n_Duque_de_Montpensier.jpg/1280px-Charro%2C_Colecci%C3%B3n_Duque_de_Montpensier.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Charro%2C_Colecci%C3%B3n_Duque_de_Montpensier.jpg/500px-Charro%2C_Colecci%C3%B3n_Duque_de_Montpensier.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Charro wearing chaparreras (ca. 1860).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACharro%2C_Colecci%C3%B3n_Duque_de_Montpensier.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Don_Alonso_Pe%C3%B3n_de_Regil%2C_Ministro_de_M%C3%A9xico_en_Italia_%281865%29.jpg/500px-Don_Alonso_Pe%C3%B3n_de_Regil%2C_Ministro_de_M%C3%A9xico_en_Italia_%281865%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Don_Alonso_Pe%C3%B3n_de_Regil%2C_Ministro_de_M%C3%A9xico_en_Italia_%281865%29.jpg/500px-Don_Alonso_Pe%C3%B3n_de_Regil%2C_Ministro_de_M%C3%A9xico_en_Italia_%281865%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Don Alonso Peón de Regil in Charro outfit with Chaparreras (1865).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADon_Alonso_Pe%C3%B3n_de_Regil%2C_Ministro_de_M%C3%A9xico_en_Italia_(1865).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Mexican_rancher.jpg/500px-Mexican_rancher.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Mexican_rancher.jpg/500px-Mexican_rancher.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mexican Ranchero wearing furry Chaparreras, probably Chivarras or goat-skin Chaparreras (1867).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMexican_rancher.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Charro_chinaco_%281866%29.jpg/500px-Charro_chinaco_%281866%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Charro_chinaco_%281866%29.jpg/500px-Charro_chinaco_%281866%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Charro Chinaco or a Mexican guerrilla fighter during the French Intervention, wearing furry Chaparreras.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACharro_chinaco_(1866).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Maximiliano_de_Habsburgo_vestido_de_Charro_%281865%29.jpg/500px-Maximiliano_de_Habsburgo_vestido_de_Charro_%281865%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Maximiliano_de_Habsburgo_vestido_de_Charro_%281865%29.jpg/500px-Maximiliano_de_Habsburgo_vestido_de_Charro_%281865%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Emperor Maximilian I of Mexico in Charro attire wearing Chaparreras, possibly of bear or otter fur (1865).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMaximiliano_de_Habsburgo_vestido_de_Charro_(1865).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Dos_Hombres_vestidos_de_Charro_%28ca._1866%29.jpg/500px-Dos_Hombres_vestidos_de_Charro_%28ca._1866%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Dos_Hombres_vestidos_de_Charro_%28ca._1866%29.jpg/500px-Dos_Hombres_vestidos_de_Charro_%28ca._1866%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Two men in Charro outfits wearing chaparreras. The man on the right has jaguar skin chaparreras (ca. 1866).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADos_Hombres_vestidos_de_Charro_(ca._1866).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Rancheros_%281844%29.jpg/500px-Rancheros_%281844%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Rancheros_%281844%29.jpg/1280px-Rancheros_%281844%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Rancheros_%281844%29.jpg/500px-Rancheros_%281844%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Ranchero, on horseback, has a set of leopard skin Armas on his saddle. When they weren't being used they simply remained hanging in front of the rider’s legs.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARancheros_(1844).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Ranchero_de_Sonora_%28_1849%29.jpg/500px-Ranchero_de_Sonora_%28_1849%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Ranchero_de_Sonora_%28_1849%29.jpg/500px-Ranchero_de_Sonora_%28_1849%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"When being used, the Armas are pulled over the legs of the rider and fastened behind the waist (1849).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARanchero_de_Sonora_(_1849).jpg"}],"sounds":{}}}